=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# backup screen-unsafe -----------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: the Backup screen. web-01.example.net runs Debian 13.$
# hardn.yml says backupPath: /tmp/hardn-backups; /tmp is world-$
# writable, so pkg/host/backup refuses it, and with it every$
# change but a new path (decision 7).$
$
# Backup Settings ##############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Backup State         Enabled$
  [ ] Backup Path          /tmp/hardn-backups Unsafe$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Backup State         Turn backups off$
   2) Backup Path          Change backup path$
   3) Verify Directory     Check the path, writing nothing$
   4) Backup Runs          None yet$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-4 or q]:$
$
$

